## Iteration 2 Questions (Feature-Focused)
Test Cards
1. Can you tell me about your experience with apps like Tinder or Bumble?
    
    a. How do you feel about the idea of swiping on people to make friends?
2. How important is it to you to know someone’s interests or hobbies before deciding to connect with them?
3. In what ways do someone’s interests or hobbies influence your decision to connect with them?
4. What kind of things on a profile would make you feel comfortable enough to start a conversation?
5. How do you feel about having a shared topic or prompt to start a conversation, and how might that affect your willingness to engage?
6. What are your thoughts on using a fun activity or game(like an iMessage game) as a way to get to know someone new, and what kind of activity would feel natural to you?
7. What group size do you feel most comfortable with when meeting new people, and why?
8. Would knowing about nearby or upcoming campus events related to your interests help you meet people in real life? How so?
9. What features would make you actually want to use a friendship app regularly?
10. What would make this app better than just using Instagram, Discord, or existing group chats?
11. What would make you feel comfortable meeting a friend you connected with through the app in real life?

